WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
SpaceX plans a $74 billion investment in supercomputing campuses to power its ai ambitions. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 161. Starshield limits from Ukraine, blue origin walking away from a NASA station contract, and rockets rolling on both coasts come next, then the engineering angle. SpaceX will split the outlay across two sites, GovCon Wire reports, putting more than $24 billion into a Texas campus next to starbase, to run large-scale

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:36.140
training and inference on the XAI and GROC stack. The Arizona site in Cochise County carries a

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:42.520
proposed $50 billion, an opposition there has gathered more than 2,400 petition signatures against

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:48.700
a component projected to create 6,500 jobs. The company says the work will grow local tax

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:54.560
bases and jobs while cleaning up debris that has sat since the 1960s. Scrap metal, discarded

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:00.640
appliances, old tanks, fiberglass insulation, construction materials, and thousands of illegally

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:06.360
dumped tires, and removal is underway as the Texas site is prepared. SpaceX is calling

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:11.840
that cleanup a chance to fix long-standing neglect, and it is positioning both campuses as shared

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:17.240
infrastructure for its own operations and the broader Musk Compute ecosystem, with coordinated

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.000
planning from the Rio Grande Valley to Cochise County along the corridor from southern Texas

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.100
to Southern Arizona.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:29.010
Ukrainian officials said speed restrictions on Starsheald, the government version of Starlink,

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:35.530
United 24 media reports, rose from 10% of missions affected on the first day to 50% on

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.930
the second, and 100% on the third.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:44.930
The limits cap speed at 161 km per hour, which they say blocks interceptor drones from matching

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:50.330
incoming Russian Sheahead threats and has complicated intercepts of jet-powered attack drones over

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.230
the front line and occupied territory.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.770
President Zelensky described the limits as systematic rather than random errors, and

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.910
Ukrainian military personnel who investigated the disruptions concluded they were not

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:02.790
technical errors.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:08.150
SpaceX stated there have been no changes to the service and told Axios the account of new

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.210
limitations as false.

00:02:10.332 --> 00:02:16.252
Dave Limp told Blue Origin employees in remarks circulating on X that the company will not bid

00:02:16.252 --> 00:02:22.412
on NASA's commercial low-earth orbit destination contract, or CLD, because its priorities remain

00:02:22.412 --> 00:02:28.092
New Glenn and Blue Moon. Blue Origin has focused resources on finishing that heavy-lift vehicle

00:02:28.092 --> 00:02:33.492
and the lunar lander, and it views the Orbital Station Award as lower priority, leaving the

00:02:33.492 --> 00:02:39.292
CLD competition to other bidders for whom it would be more consequential. A contest industry observers

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:45.639
say carries greater weight for smaller commercial providers. Brownsville is receiving $220 million

00:02:45.639 --> 00:02:50.939
dollars from SpaceX, pledged on X as the largest private contribution in the city's history,

00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:54.839
aimed at long-term drinking water reliability around starbase.

00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:59.959
The funds will support water and wastewater systems serving Brownsville and Cameron County,

00:03:00.419 --> 00:03:05.359
framed as part of broader Rio Grande Valley infrastructure work that expands supply capacity

00:03:05.359 --> 00:03:11.198
for generations of residents in one of the region's most pressing challenges. To the new is working

00:03:11.198 --> 00:03:17.658
with SpaceX SI, SMB tech reports, to put the cursor coding platform inside larger companies

00:03:17.658 --> 00:03:22.458
that already run GROC. The collaboration is built for organizations trying to scale

00:03:22.458 --> 00:03:27.958
agent-based development, so teams can hand tasks across multiple users and agents in shared

00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:32.978
workspaces, and it pushes GROC further into enterprise coding through the cursor interface.

00:03:34.032 --> 00:03:37.332
Cape Canaveral has a Vulcan on the pad, Florida Today reports,

00:03:37.332 --> 00:03:42.572
efforts, as United Launch Alliance rolls the VC-6L configuration for Friday's Amazon

00:03:42.572 --> 00:03:45.892
Leo LV-01 mission from SLC-41.

00:03:46.452 --> 00:03:51.472
That stack is the most powerful Vulcan flown yet, lifting for Amazon's project Kuiper

00:03:51.472 --> 00:03:57.172
build out on the same day Starship Flight 15 is scheduled from Texas, November 13 on both

00:03:57.172 --> 00:03:57.712
manifests.

00:03:58.861 --> 00:04:04.061
In a separate commitment, SpaceX is backing a child protection initiative with 750 free

00:04:04.061 --> 00:04:09.601
Starlink kits, drive Tesla Canada reports, that will connect children's homes across Africa.

00:04:10.141 --> 00:04:15.301
NASA Space Flight posted updated imagery of ship 42 being lifted and moved to the launch

00:04:15.301 --> 00:04:15.561
mount.

00:04:16.041 --> 00:04:20.581
The upper stage in the final stacking sequence at Starbase ahead of the planned flight 15

00:04:20.581 --> 00:04:21.021
window.

00:04:21.581 --> 00:04:27.081
Starship Gaser in a post not yet confirmed by the company had ship 42 rolled out to pad

00:04:27.081 --> 00:04:31.501
two and stacked atop booster 22 with about 24 hours remaining.

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:37.278
the clock at T-24 and a half hours. Worth keeping an eye on is the European

00:04:37.278 --> 00:04:42.338
Commission's call. Key of post reports for SpaceX to restore full star-shield

00:04:42.338 --> 00:04:46.838
operations as soon as possible after President Zelensky said the speed cap has

00:04:46.838 --> 00:04:51.578
already allowed some Russian strikes to penetrate defenses. The dispute raises a

00:04:51.578 --> 00:04:55.318
fair operational question when a foreign government is using the network for

00:04:55.318 --> 00:05:00.898
real-time intercepts. How fast a contested limit can be checked or lifted. A shared

00:05:00.898 --> 00:05:05.638
Their telemetry record, or a confirmed return to unrestricted speeds, is what would settle

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:05.858
it.

00:05:06.722 --> 00:05:10.242
For the vehicle now on the clock, the engineering angle is a double catch.

00:05:10.942 --> 00:05:16.042
The ship upper stage has to live through a full orbital mission, 14 revolutions, and

00:05:16.042 --> 00:05:21.242
a high energy reentry before threading itself between the tower arms, roughly 22 hours

00:05:21.242 --> 00:05:25.062
after launch, while the booster is already back in six and a half minutes.

00:05:25.642 --> 00:05:30.922
The first stage already has three tower catches and never reaches orbital speed, so its heat

00:05:30.922 --> 00:05:37.162
pulse is a short slap next to the upper stages, low-earth orbit moves at roughly 8 km per second,

00:05:37.642 --> 00:05:42.962
and a circuit takes on the order of 90 minutes. A back-of-envelope figure puts kinetic energy

00:05:42.962 --> 00:05:48.802
near 32 megajoules in every kilogram of the ship at that speed, almost all of it dumped as heat

00:05:48.802 --> 00:05:54.142
in the shock layer before the tower ever sees the vehicle. Heading climbs on the order of velocity

00:05:54.142 --> 00:05:59.842
cubed, so the ship sees far higher peak heating while still needing tiles intact for immediate reuse,

00:05:59.842 --> 00:06:05.162
which is why the first block three ships flew with extra instrumentation and thicker tile bonds.

00:06:05.802 --> 00:06:10.542
Catching both stages without ocean recovery is how the cost of the next flight falls toward

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:16.922
the propellant bill. Each avoided splashdown drops weeks of logistics, saltwater exposure and tile

00:06:16.922 --> 00:06:23.022
replacement labor. Treat methane, oxygen, and metal as the magic wand inputs and the fluids for a

00:06:23.022 --> 00:06:28.862
vehicle this size sit on a back of envelope figure in the low millions of dollars at commodity prices.

00:06:28.862 --> 00:06:29.022
charges.

00:06:29.442 --> 00:06:35.062
Every recovery ship, barge, and depot-level tile swap is the idiot index, the factor

00:06:35.062 --> 00:06:37.862
by which the real operation exceeds those raw inputs.

00:06:38.482 --> 00:06:44.202
An 80-year goal on a 124-meter stack only works if the upper-stage heat shield and

00:06:44.202 --> 00:06:47.862
the legless catch can match the reliability the booster has already shown.

00:06:48.482 --> 00:06:53.962
Flight's 12-14 showed progressive gains in ascent engine reliability and payload deployment,

00:06:54.402 --> 00:06:55.322
and they set the bar.

00:06:55.322 --> 00:07:01.662
flight-12's first block-3 booster had boostback trouble, the burn that turns it around toward the tower,

00:07:02.162 --> 00:07:07.422
and was lost in the landing-burn. While ship-39 lost a Raptor vacuum, the vacuum

00:07:07.422 --> 00:07:12.862
optimized upper-stage engine on a scent yet still deployed its payload into an on-target Indian

00:07:12.862 --> 00:07:19.162
ocean splash-down. Flight-13's booster-20 flew a clean ascent and boostback before ice ingestion

00:07:19.162 --> 00:07:25.282
shorten the landing burn into a gulf impact, and ship 40 flew cleanly, deployed 20 Starling

00:07:25.282 --> 00:07:31.822
V3 satellites, and returned intact for tile study. Flight 14, the first orbital starship mission,

00:07:32.322 --> 00:07:38.842
saw booster 21 lose two Raptors and still splash down soft, and ship 41 lose one Raptor vacuum,

00:07:39.342 --> 00:07:45.642
deployed 26 Starling V3 satellites, and fly a contingency reentry. Every one of those boosters

00:07:45.642 --> 00:07:49.262
still had at least one engine anomaly during boost back or landing.

00:07:49.842 --> 00:07:54.822
Flight 15 has to clear that on both stages to claim the first fully reusable orbital launch

00:07:54.822 --> 00:07:55.242
system.

00:07:55.902 --> 00:07:59.282
Shares were barely higher on the day, up a fraction of a percent.

